{"base_rate":0.4687022900763359,"brier":0.1175363358778626,"bss":0.5280052931596091,"bss_hi":0.5897720826860996,"bss_lo":0.4601242145955581,"chart":{"base":[669.8,94.1],"fp":[281.2,346.1],"lead":"62,222.1 272,175.9 482,123.7 692,33.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.53 — higher than 93% of cities","fp":"low end +8pp, high end +3pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.4 °C — better than 24% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 9%; promised 100% → rained 96%"},"rel":"74.3,426.4 279.4,294.5 581.5,118.4 691.8,53.3"},"country":"RU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.053175572519083995,"ess":333.90991935826764,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tobolsk</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tobolsk rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>96%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>7%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 655 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nTOBOLSK, 5.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.53, ranked 10 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(5&ndash;24) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>176</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>93%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>96%</b></td><td class='num'>134</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tobolsk</b> <span class=\"muted\">RU</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.53</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>5&ndash;24\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>655 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tobolsk &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tobolsk\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.06034090909091,379.9318181818182 78.86953488372092,339.6744186046512 140.636875,256.875 217.93402985074627,175.55223880597015 310.874,78.66666666666663 384.30470588235295,28.572058823530142 411.89432835820895,18.0 411.89432835820895,20.716417910447774 384.30470588235295,71.52941176470591 310.874,163.6 217.93402985074627,257.04477611940297 140.636875,330.8125 78.86953488372092,377.7674418604651 58.06034090909091,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"211.39236641221373\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"211.39236641221373\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.06034090909091,357.1818181818182 78.86953488372092,331.2093023255814 140.636875,273.9375 217.93402985074627,202.71641791044777 310.874,139.33333333333334 384.30470588235295,44.76470588235293 411.89432835820895,34.29850746268659\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 176 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.06034090909091\" cy=\"357.1818181818182\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"78.86953488372092\" cy=\"331.2093023255814\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 23%&amp;#10;It rained 30% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"140.636875\" cy=\"273.9375\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"217.93402985074627\" cy=\"202.71641791044777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 60 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"310.874\" cy=\"139.33333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 93% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"384.30470588235295\" cy=\"44.76470588235293\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 96% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 134 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.89432835820895\" cy=\"34.29850746268659\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(47%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Tobolsk the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.60) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.49).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'>0.488</td><td class='num'>12.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.503</td><td class='num'>6.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>169</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.506</td><td class='num'>6.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>143</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.595</td><td class='num'>6.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":58.19807,"lon":68.25457,"n":655,"n_cities":134,"name":"Tobolsk","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00017045454545454544,"n":176,"obs":0.06818181818181818,"sig":true},{"hi":0.13200000000000045,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.058953488372092994,"n":86,"obs":0.13953488372093023,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.13200000000000045,"mean":0.23343750000000002,"n":64,"obs":0.296875,"sig":false},{"hi":0.5940000000000003,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.4517910447761194,"n":67,"obs":0.4925373134328358,"sig":false},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.5940000000000003,"mean":0.7143333333333335,"n":60,"obs":0.6666666666666666,"sig":false},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.9217647058823529,"n":68,"obs":0.9264705882352942,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9997014925373134,"n":134,"obs":0.9552238805970149,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.3,"provisional":false,"rank":10,"rank_hi":24.0,"rank_lo":5.0,"reliability":0.003273645453605098,"resolution":0.1340432429841062,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"tobolsk","station":"TOBOLSK","timezone":"Asia/Yekaterinburg"}